{
  "_readme": [
    "MasriVoice — THE Egyptian navigation phrasebook. One file, three consumers:",
    "  tools/masri_voice/masri_voice.py (reference + desk harnesses + the clip-bank builder),",
    "  android nav/MasriPhrases.kt and ios/Runner/MasriPhrases.swift (GENERATED from this file by",
    "  tools/masri_voice/gen_tables.py — never edit them by hand; tool/masri_voice_parity.py fails on drift).",
    "Every spoken Arabic navigation line is COMPOSED from these segments using the maneuver DATA",
    "(type / modifier / exit / degrees / distance) — never by rewriting the provider's Arabic text.",
    "A composed line is its segments joined by U+2063 (INVISIBLE SEPARATOR) and led by one; each",
    "segment has a pre-rendered clip in assets/voice/ar/ (the bank), so the line plays with no network.",
    "Variants: a list per key; a variant is one string (both genders) or {m, f} (the addressee's gender).",
    "The SPEAKER is a woman (the bank's voice): words about herself are feminine — صاحية, حاسباها.",
    "U-turn is «لف وارجع» / «اعمل لفّة وارجع» (2026-10-11: «اعمل ملف» reads as 'make a file' and no Egyptian says it — the",
    "user; «الدوران» is avoided because a roundabout is الصينية / الميدان and the two must never be confused). The loanword «يوتيرن» came back",
    "from the ASR read-back as «يوتيوبر» / «ريفيو»; «لفّي وارجعي» was once heard as «لف يمين» — pronounce.py diacritizes it and the phone listener gates the take.",
    "Doc: docs/egyptian-voice-2026-09.md (inventory, the case -> phrase mapping, the voice choice).",
    "STAGES (2026-10-11, 'no detail twice'): the FIRST line that names a maneuver gives the whole picture (approach / final keys); once the driver has been told (MasriVoice.Told — per route, per leg), a later approach line says only the reminder (*.remind: «بعد ميتين متر، هتخش شمال») and the line at the maneuver only what is needed NOW (*.now: «دلوقتي يمين», a roundabout's exit «خُد تالت مخرج»). A reroute is a new route: the picture is given again."
  ],
